Newton’s method finds roots of \(f(x)=0\) by repeatedly linearizing: from \(x_n\), it follows the tangent line at \((x_n, f(x_n))\) to its \(x\)-intercept,
\[
x_{n+1}=x_n-\frac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)}.
\]

