Fixed point iteration solves \(x=g(x)\) by repeatedly applying \(g\): \(x_{n+1}=g(x_n)\). If the sequence converges to a value \(\alpha\), then \(\alpha=g(\alpha)\) — a fixed point of \(g\).

// VM is the shared utility library, loaded globally via _includes/head-scripts.html (js/**). This page uses VM.numerical.linearRegression (L2), VM.numerical.l1Regression (L1), VM.plotting.paddedRange, VM.ui.renderTable.
